}


AKS Platform Admin

Description:
This role provides full administrative access to AKS clusters and namespaces, combining cluster-level and namespace-level management capabilities. Users can:

Read and list cluster credentials (admin, user, monitoring)

Manage all cluster resources (Pods, Deployments, DaemonSets, StatefulSets, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, Jobs, CronJobs, Namespaces, Network Policies, etc.)

Run commands against the cluster

Read role assignments and resource groups

Key Points:

Grants both cluster-wide and namespace-wide management.

Enables operational tasks like deploying workloads, modifying namespace resources, and accessing Secrets.

Suitable for platform engineers or operators who manage AKS infrastructure.

Custom Role 2: AKS Platform Reader

Description:
This role provides read-only access across AKS clusters and namespaces, combining the data-reading capabilities from multiple built-in AKS reader roles. Users can:

Read cluster credentials (user, monitoring)

View cluster and namespace resources (Pods, Deployments, DaemonSets, Services, ConfigMaps, Jobs, CronJobs, Network Policies, ResourceQuotas, etc.)

Read role assignments and resource groups

Key Points:

No ability to modify any resources.

Can be assigned at cluster scope for cross-namespace read access.

Ideal for auditors, developers, or monitoring tools that need visibility without write permissions.

In short:

Admin role: Full control at cluster and namespace level.

Reader role: Full visibility at cluster and namespace level, no write access.
